        "problem": "$\\int ({sec}^{2}\u2061x-2csc\u2061xcot\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int csc\u2061xcot\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =-csc\u2061x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =tan\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sec}^{2}\u2061x-2csc\u2061xcot\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int csc\u2061xcot\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =tan\u2061x-2(-csc\u2061x)+C \\\\  & =tan\u2061x+2csc\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
